WEBVTT

00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:08.390
We're finally hunting oni!

00:00:08.390 --> 00:00:11.010
Let's make sure we bag our 
first prize this time!

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:11.920
Yeah.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.400
We're a pair of guys who 
share the same dream.

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:16.990
<b>Day 1</b>

00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:16.960
No matter what happens on this trip...

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:20.160
We'll get along with no fighting!

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.970
Get along with no fighting!

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:27.330
<b>Day 3</b>

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:35.600
Get along...

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:36.690
With no fighting.

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:41.140
<b>Day 7</b>

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:43.990
Get along...

00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:45.610
With no fighting...

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:49.960
Get along...

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:51.600
With no fighting...

00:00:55.810 --> 00:00:58.150
Man, I'm hungry...

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:02.810
Dammit, why didn't you come 
up with more food, Kojiro?!

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:06.160
Get along... with no fighting...

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:07.540
Get along...

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:10.130
I'm thirsty and I'm starving!

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:15.560
Quit whining when you're the one who
 left all the prep to me, you sheltered punk!

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:17.560
I'm sheltered?!

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:21.270
You don't know anything 
about the outside world either!

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:24.720
I had to survive on my own after my dad died.

00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:30.180
I didn't get waited on hand and foot
 in the miner dorms like you!

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:32.650
I've got powers you don't.

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:34.110
Powers?

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:35.870
Like what?

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:42.370
The power...

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:48.280
of self-sufficiency.

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:54.200
How many did you catch, Musashi?

00:01:55.910 --> 00:01:58.780
Why, it couldn't be zero, could it?

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:03.470
What's your problem, fisher-samurai?!

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:06.430
I'm gonna catch just as many! 
You wait and see!

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:11.170
What am I doing?

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:15.820
He tries a lot harder when 
it comes to hunting oni...

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:17.840
And now I'm competing with him over this?

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:21.030
So what if I'm better at fishing?

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:23.830
I'm disappointed with myself...

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:03.380
<b>The Kosameda Band</b>

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:03.430
I'm not catching squat...

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:06.820
I guess I <i>did</i> leave getting stuff 
together for the trip to Kojiro.

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:13.380
Why are we fighting over food?

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:18.140
Kojiro... I'm sorry.

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:20.990
Let's eat lunch together. Huh?

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:23.940
Kojiro? Where'd you go?

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:25.660
Hey!

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:29.110
Kojiro?!

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:33.800
That's a sword wound!

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:35.810
Who did this to you?!

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:37.640
That woman...

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:39.790
What'd you say?

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:54.820
Hand over all your valuables.

00:04:56.010 --> 00:04:57.400
Did you not hear me?

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:59.170
I want your valuables.

00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:03.180
Give me your Kitetsu. Now.

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:05.470
Our Kitetsu?

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:07.960
Are you the one who hurt Kojiro?

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:08.820
That's right.

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:12.950
And if you resist, I'll mess 
you up just like blondie.

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:16.490
I see...

00:05:16.490 --> 00:05:17.790
What? You wanna do this?

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:19.580
Where's your sword?

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:22.630
I won't need one against you!

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:41.670
What?

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.950
You're little and light.

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:48.570
Both you <i>and</i> your punches!

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:54.990
I'm taking your head off!

00:05:58.270 --> 00:05:59.200
Bye now.

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:00.790
Man, that smarts!

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:03.050
Why didn't it work?!

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:05.270
You...

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:07.760
You're definitely something else.

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:12.210
<i>But she's not </i>that<i> strong. 
How did she beat Kojiro?</i>

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:14.520
If that didn't do it, then...

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:17.170
You're really handsome.

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:20.070
What's this? A change of heart?

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:22.650
Be careful, Musashi!

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:27.100
I just love strong men like you...

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:28.470
What?!

00:06:28.470 --> 00:06:30.770
Don't do it! Put those away!

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:35.250
If it was with you, I wouldn't 
mind anything you had in mind...

00:06:35.590 --> 00:06:39.900
Anything I want...?

00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:44.700
You fell for it, stupid!

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:48.190
You're just as easy as him! 
And wide open!

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:51.120
No openings here!

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:57.490
Blondie was weak in the knees
 after just a glimpse...

00:06:57.490 --> 00:07:00.820
Did her little seduction act
seriously get you, Kojiro?

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:03.780
Shut up! I just let my guard down!

00:07:04.140 --> 00:07:06.960
Sorry, but sex appeal 
isn't gonna work on me.

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:11.200
I had special training against it
 when I was a miner.

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:13.150
Special training?!

00:07:13.150 --> 00:07:15.630
I guess I better get serious, then.

00:07:23.990 --> 00:07:26.180
What kind of weapon is that?

00:07:30.610 --> 00:07:32.320
It's past noon already!

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:34.260
My lord is gonna be furious!

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:37.100
Kojiro?

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:38.590
I'm borrowing this!

00:07:42.550 --> 00:07:45.310
She just rode off with our steel horse!

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:46.310
Let's get it back!

00:07:46.310 --> 00:07:48.020
Right! After her!

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:56.910
<b>Kosameda Band</b>

00:07:57.330 --> 00:07:59.790
I am so sorry I'm late, my lord!

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:03.260
Um, Your Lordship?

00:08:04.230 --> 00:08:08.720
What's this? Did we have a girl who can't
 even keep appointments in this band?

00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:10.360
I'm so sorry!

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:15.170
But I stole the Kitetsu Mount from 
the Bushi, just as you instructed!

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:19.880
I knew you could do it if you tried. 
Just what I'd expect from my girl.

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:22.600
Now come here!

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:24.220
My lord!

00:08:25.320 --> 00:08:28.270
I love you so much, my lord!

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:32.990
Please, give me my next orders.

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:35.010
Should I be on standby?

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:36.470
Should I train?

00:08:36.470 --> 00:08:38.250
Or is there a mission?

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:44.160
<b>Kosameda Band Captain
Kosameda Hideo</b>

00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:41.060
Your mission is to hunt oni, of course.

00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:43.570
So that, one day, we can reunite the nation.

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:49.130
<b>Kosameda Band Member 
Hattori Tsugumi</b>

00:08:44.450 --> 00:08:46.750
Of course, my lord!

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:56.620
I can't believe that rotten wench 
made off with all our stuff!

00:08:56.620 --> 00:08:57.910
She's gonna pay!

00:08:57.910 --> 00:09:00.100
I've never seen a girl 
up close like that before!

00:09:00.730 --> 00:09:02.550
Is this where she went?

00:09:02.550 --> 00:09:06.310
Hey, look, Musashi. 
It says "Kosameda Band."

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:07.520
<b>Kosameda Band</b>

00:09:06.310 --> 00:09:07.510
Yeah, you're right!

00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:09.470
A Bushi band?

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:14.160
Come to think of it, the Takeda Band
 had a fortress like this, too.

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:17.590
A bunch of them came flying out of it...

00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:20.550
There must be a bunch 
of Bushi in this one, too.

00:09:20.550 --> 00:09:24.450
No telling what they're like,
but we gotta go in anyway.

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:27.570
My dad left me that steel horse.

00:09:27.570 --> 00:09:29.430
Then we'd better get it back!

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:33.390
This place is huge...

00:09:34.730 --> 00:09:37.100
Where did she hide it?!

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:40.240
Over here.

00:09:41.020 --> 00:09:43.810
On behalf of the Kosameda Band, welcome!

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:48.130
Hey, you thief! Return my steel horse!

00:09:48.130 --> 00:09:51.140
You can have it right back! 
I was just borrowing it!

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:52.410
Come right this way!

00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:55.310
Come along! Follow me!

00:09:55.310 --> 00:09:56.120
That's suspicious.

00:09:56.390 --> 00:09:59.670
She's gotta be up to something again.

00:09:59.670 --> 00:10:00.780
Let's be careful.

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:01.580
Right.

00:10:02.030 --> 00:10:04.290
Your Kitetsu Mount is right this way.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:06.540
Look at that!

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:13.510
There's a town inside of the fortress!

00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:16.220
It's technically a castle, y'know.

00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:19.900
What is?

00:10:19.900 --> 00:10:22.440
You guys have never seen 
a Bushi band's castle before?

00:10:22.440 --> 00:10:24.030
We have from the outside.

00:10:24.030 --> 00:10:26.260
But it flew off pretty quick.

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:29.140
Well, that's what makes it special.

00:10:29.140 --> 00:10:31.230
Bushi band castles can travel.

00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:34.060
They travel? How's that work?

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:39.260
Kishin pop up all over the country!

00:10:39.260 --> 00:10:44.000
And Bushi bands will track them down,
no matter where they are.

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:47.900
The people who live here 
make that all possible.

00:10:47.900 --> 00:10:49.800
We have retainers, weapon craftsmen,

00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:51.850
tenant farmers who cultivate food...

00:10:51.850 --> 00:10:54.470
Plus combat medics and 
people who raise livestock!

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:58.310
People have been living like 
this for over a century.

00:10:58.310 --> 00:11:00.880
Bushi bands are like giant families
 that fight together!

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:07.510
That's amazing... So the entire 
town comes along for the oni fights?

00:11:07.940 --> 00:11:09.340
They've got crops...

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:11.670
and even a temple school!

00:11:11.670 --> 00:11:12.440
Yep!

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:14.360
The kids of the band members go there.

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:16.660
Hey, it's Tsugumi!

00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:17.560
You're right!

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:22.670
Gosh, are you two skipping
 sword training again?

00:11:22.670 --> 00:11:24.730
You should help us practice!

00:11:24.730 --> 00:11:26.550
I'm gonna land a hit on you today!

00:11:26.550 --> 00:11:29.170
You seriously think you can beat me?

00:11:39.980 --> 00:11:42.430
Takes you back, doesn't it?

00:11:42.980 --> 00:11:43.970
Yeah.

00:11:45.380 --> 00:11:46.610
Sure does.

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:52.030
Come on, more!

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:52.830
Yeah, more!

00:11:52.830 --> 00:11:56.830
I can't! You two are getting bigger.

00:11:56.830 --> 00:11:58.080
Could you switch with me?

00:11:58.080 --> 00:11:59.120
Who, me?

00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:00.780
Come on, come on!

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:02.860
Play with the kids, Kojiro.

00:12:03.540 --> 00:12:05.330
I guess I have to...

00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:09.010
Come!

00:12:10.840 --> 00:12:14.750
I thought that Bushi would 
be fighting oni every day...

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:18.720
But I guess that's not the case. 
There're normal families here.

00:12:19.030 --> 00:12:21.160
Normal families, huh?

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:25.770
I know I said that Bushi bands 
are like big families,

00:12:26.190 --> 00:12:30.170
but I don't have any blood relatives here.

00:12:46.170 --> 00:12:48.160
Big Sis Tsubame!

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:57.160
Uniting the country would be wonderful.

00:12:57.920 --> 00:13:00.230
But we don't just fight for ourselves.

00:13:00.230 --> 00:13:03.820
We're also doing this to protect people 
who are weaker than us.

00:13:04.340 --> 00:13:06.670
That's the Bushi way, Tsugumi.

00:13:06.940 --> 00:13:07.770
Yeah!

00:13:07.770 --> 00:13:11.560
I'm gonna be a nice Bushi like you, Tsubame!

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:16.090
Big Sis!

00:13:18.720 --> 00:13:22.200
All of mine are dead.

00:13:26.480 --> 00:13:29.560
I guess you're like me, then.

00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:37.670
Hey, Musashi, would you tag in already?!

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:39.520
Yeah, I'm on it!

00:13:44.250 --> 00:13:47.050
Who does he think he is?

00:13:50.090 --> 00:13:51.440
Weirdo.

00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:53.970
You seem to be getting along.

00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:57.030
Y-Yes!

00:14:00.500 --> 00:14:01.870
My lord...

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:09.500
The Kosameda Band welcomes you,

00:14:10.690 --> 00:14:12.490
Sir Musashi, Sir Kojiro.

00:14:14.130 --> 00:14:18.970
I am Kosameda Hideo, 
the captain of the Kosameda Band.

00:14:18.970 --> 00:14:21.870
I'd be delighted to make a 
pair of new Bushi allies.

00:14:22.180 --> 00:14:24.770
The captain here seems like a nice guy!

00:14:25.150 --> 00:14:26.850
You don't think this is weird?

00:14:27.250 --> 00:14:30.310
Why roll out this whole feast for us?

00:14:30.310 --> 00:14:32.580
Don't worry about it! Just eat up!

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:34.440
Here! Say "ah!"

00:14:34.440 --> 00:14:35.610
Uh, I'm good...

00:14:35.610 --> 00:14:40.120
I must say, I've had a look 
at your Kitetsu Mount,

00:14:40.120 --> 00:14:43.710
and for it to be such a fine vehicle,

00:14:43.710 --> 00:14:48.900
you two must be first-rate Bushi 
who've slain many a Kishin.

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:53.160
So I'd like to make you a proposal...

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:57.130
Would you be willing to fight 
alongside the Kosameda Band?

00:14:57.130 --> 00:14:58.620
Alongside you?

00:14:58.620 --> 00:15:04.080
Yes. There's a great number 
of stray oni in this area.

00:15:04.570 --> 00:15:07.550
By working together,
 we can minimize casualties.

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:09.890
Then we can split the Kitetsu afterward.

00:15:09.890 --> 00:15:12.040
And what's that?

00:15:15.420 --> 00:15:18.800
You mean... you don't know what Kitetsu is?

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:21.020
Can't say we do.

00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:21.820
Yeah.

00:15:22.870 --> 00:15:27.730
Well, you two are useless then.

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:30.550
Tsugumi.

00:15:30.550 --> 00:15:31.820
But, Your Lordship, they...

00:15:32.300 --> 00:15:33.650
Just tie them up. Now.

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:35.940
Y-Yes, sir.

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:37.690
What?

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:42.680
Kitetsu Blade: Twin Soaring Swallows!

00:15:50.540 --> 00:15:51.770
What the—?!

00:15:52.040 --> 00:15:54.970
I can't even cut it with my sword!

00:15:55.320 --> 00:15:57.480
Hey! Let us go!

00:15:57.480 --> 00:15:58.390
I'm sorry.

00:15:59.710 --> 00:16:01.890
I-I'm so sorry...

00:16:04.420 --> 00:16:08.470
They were still in possession 
of a fine mount.

00:16:08.470 --> 00:16:11.990
They may have more Kitetsu 
hidden somewhere.

00:16:12.470 --> 00:16:14.090
Let's lock them up.

00:16:16.860 --> 00:16:17.910
I'm sorry.

00:16:19.060 --> 00:16:22.870
If I hadn't been so stupid and useless...

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:24.380
Say it again.

00:16:25.490 --> 00:16:28.060
I'm stupid and useless...

00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:30.460
I can't hear you. Again.

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:33.620
I failed because I'm stupid and useless!

00:16:33.980 --> 00:16:39.000
The mission was to bring powerful Bushi 
who would be of use to you, and yet...

00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:42.460
You really are a worthless 
daughter, aren't you?

00:16:42.970 --> 00:16:47.140
Does that feeble brain of yours even 
comprehend the situation we're in?

00:16:47.570 --> 00:16:48.450
Yes.

00:16:49.540 --> 00:16:51.240
After successive battles against oni,

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:53.890
we're running low on band members and Kitetsu...

00:16:55.840 --> 00:17:01.130
But Lord Tokugawa entrusted this land to me,
 and I intend to defend it at any cost.

00:17:01.690 --> 00:17:04.500
The next time the oni attack...

00:17:07.620 --> 00:17:09.880
I may have to call for total 
mobilization of the castle town.

00:17:10.700 --> 00:17:13.550
T-Total mobilization, sir?!

00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:14.340
That's right.

00:17:14.850 --> 00:17:19.650
But most of the adults are 
women and senior citizens.

00:17:21.430 --> 00:17:23.740
And that's not to mention the children...

00:17:24.660 --> 00:17:29.740
Isn't it cruel to expect them 
to be willing to fight oni to the death?!

00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:36.150
Is it really?

00:17:38.140 --> 00:17:42.210
Bushi bands were created to fight oni.

00:17:42.590 --> 00:17:48.570
Shouldn't it be a Bushi's greatest joy to 
fight to the last man in a stand against oni?

00:17:48.830 --> 00:17:50.190
B-But, sir...

00:17:50.190 --> 00:17:53.300
But what? If you've got an 
argument, let's hear it.

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:54.690
Well?

00:17:55.100 --> 00:17:55.860
Well?

00:17:56.240 --> 00:17:57.100
Well?

00:18:01.460 --> 00:18:02.540
What's wrong?

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:06.010
I asked you if you had an argument!

00:18:06.010 --> 00:18:07.980
You little imbecile!

00:18:12.680 --> 00:18:15.340
No. You're right, of course.

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:20.780
Please give me orders, my lord.

00:18:21.840 --> 00:18:25.060
What should I do?

00:18:25.060 --> 00:18:26.320
Should I be on standby?

00:18:26.320 --> 00:18:27.790
Should I train?

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:29.610
Or is there a mission?

00:18:31.740 --> 00:18:36.250
You really are worthless 
without me, Tsugumi.

00:18:36.520 --> 00:18:37.350
Yes, sir.

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:43.680
You've really never been much use...

00:18:43.940 --> 00:18:48.400
I'm sorry. I'm trying, but...

00:18:48.800 --> 00:18:50.880
You don't need to try.

00:18:52.240 --> 00:18:54.710
I'll always be with you.

00:18:55.070 --> 00:18:57.990
So you just need to do as I tell you.

00:18:58.600 --> 00:19:01.540
Yes, my lord...

00:19:03.770 --> 00:19:08.060
Dammit. That stupid, poker-faced clown...

00:19:08.060 --> 00:19:11.110
I can't believe he threw us in here.

00:19:17.390 --> 00:19:20.220
Yoohoo! You two doing well?

00:19:20.690 --> 00:19:21.500
You...

00:19:22.480 --> 00:19:24.780
What happened to your face?

00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:27.600
All cried out

00:19:25.220 --> 00:19:27.600
You're a total mess.

00:19:27.940 --> 00:19:31.730
And isn't she acting kind of weird?

00:19:32.060 --> 00:19:33.100
Yeah.

00:19:33.290 --> 00:19:36.590
Say, I need to ask you guys something!

00:19:36.590 --> 00:19:38.810
You actually do have some Kitetsu, right?

00:19:38.810 --> 00:19:41.810
What even is this Kitetsu 
stuff you keep talking about?

00:19:42.470 --> 00:19:44.400
You really don't know?

00:19:44.400 --> 00:19:46.720
It's written with the characters for "oni" 
and "iron", and read as "Kitetsu."

00:19:46.720 --> 00:19:48.700
It comes from the bodies of oni!

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:50.800
The bodies of oni?

00:19:51.230 --> 00:19:56.320
Yeah! You know how they
 break apart when they die?

00:19:56.320 --> 00:19:59.000
Well, that sparkly iron sand is Kitetsu!

00:19:59.000 --> 00:20:01.780
<i>We're absorbing the Kishin's power.</i>

00:20:02.630 --> 00:20:04.510
Oh, that stuff.

00:20:04.510 --> 00:20:07.170
Kitetsu has strange powers,

00:20:07.170 --> 00:20:10.470
and Bushi use those powers to fight oni.

00:20:10.470 --> 00:20:13.210
That's why we need it for the big battle.

00:20:13.640 --> 00:20:14.470
What big battle?

00:20:15.140 --> 00:20:18.950
A herd of kodama oni are 
headed to the castle...

00:20:19.350 --> 00:20:22.440
Those must be the strong 
wild oni that Kosameda mentioned.

00:20:22.440 --> 00:20:24.420
The ones he wanted our help against...

00:20:24.860 --> 00:20:25.640
But...

00:20:26.890 --> 00:20:29.790
At this rate... everyone's...

00:20:31.600 --> 00:20:35.380
Listen, what are you keeping bottled up?

00:20:36.060 --> 00:20:37.410
Look at your hands.

00:20:40.680 --> 00:20:42.830
Am I... bottling something up?

00:20:43.660 --> 00:20:46.210
There's nothing... really...

00:20:46.550 --> 00:20:49.740
I don't know why you're keeping quiet,

00:20:50.010 --> 00:20:52.360
but if there's something you gotta get out,

00:20:53.380 --> 00:20:55.350
why not just say it?

00:20:58.410 --> 00:21:01.850
Something... I need to get out?

00:21:03.340 --> 00:21:07.210
<i>I... don't want the townspeople to die.</i>

00:21:08.010 --> 00:21:11.580
<i>I'm opposed to mobilizing everyone!</i>

00:21:12.190 --> 00:21:15.350
<i>I... say no!</i>

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:17.730
<i>I'm against it!</i>

00:21:19.510 --> 00:21:20.660
H-Hey...

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:28.050
Don't make me think about this stuff!

00:21:28.050 --> 00:21:29.170
Hey, wait up!

00:21:29.720 --> 00:21:32.840
<i>I was having bad thoughts!</i>

00:21:32.840 --> 00:21:34.970
<i>I can't think like that!</i>

00:21:34.970 --> 00:21:37.740
<i>It's their fault that my 
head's all messed up!</i>

00:21:37.740 --> 00:21:42.500
<i>What should I do?! Someone tell me!</i>

00:21:42.500 --> 00:21:43.890
<i>Anyone!</i>

00:21:46.070 --> 00:21:48.130
You think she's okay?

00:23:25.330 --> 00:23:27.950
Hey, what was that 
"special training" you mentioned?

00:23:27.950 --> 00:23:31.150
They trained us to purge obtrusive thoughts
 that would distract us while mining!

00:23:31.150 --> 00:23:33.170
Hey, miner! Go out with me!

00:23:33.170 --> 00:23:33.850
Wha?!

00:23:33.850 --> 00:23:35.970
If a girl comes after you, 
you toss her like this!

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:38.090
It's part of the miner's code!

00:23:37.730 --> 00:23:40.050
<b>Next Time
Choosing Tomorrow</b>

00:23:38.090 --> 00:23:40.010
Being a miner sounds rough...
